# Handle Widget Visibility in newInstance

**Rule:** When a section can be fully hidden based on Bloc/Cubit state (e.g. the API returns empty), decide whether to build it inside the `newInstance` factory (using `Builder` + `context.watch`) instead of always building the widget and returning `SizedBox.shrink()` from its `build`. This avoids inserting an empty widget into the tree.

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final state = context.watch<MyCubit>().state;
  if (state.isEmpty) {
    return const SizedBox.shrink(); // empty widget still mounted
  }
  return Column(...);
}
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
static Widget newInstance({Key? key}) {
  return BlocProvider<MyCubit>(
    create: (_) => MyCubit()..init(),
    child: Builder(
      builder: (context) {
        final state = context.watch<MyCubit>().state;
        if (state.status.isSuccess) return MySection._(key: key);
        return const SizedBox.shrink();
      },
    ),
  );
}
```
